# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# Every unmatched path (deep links, hard refreshes of /journey, /habits, …,
# and the OAuth code return landing on /?code=…&state=…) must serve index.html
# with a 200 so the React Router can render the route. Exact static-file
# matches (assets/*, sw.js, logo.png, …) are served directly and never pass
# through this rule.
#
# The wrangler assets worker (root wrangler.jsonc) uses
# `assets.not_found_handling: single-page-application` for the same behavior;
# this file makes a Cloudflare Pages deployment behave identically without
# relying on dashboard settings.
/*	/index.html	200
